% Goal

Implement and maintain `hands/stem_layer.py`. Performs a brain.stem_layer_plan plan live through the Mixxx control API. Refuses (LayerRefused) a running mix/audition (hands.audition_transition.running_mix_processes, which also lists this module) or playing decks unless take_over. Deck 1 instrumental from its cue with set_bpm_target to the vocal's tempo; deck 2 vocal at rate 0 (the voice is never stretched); quantize and sync off on both (no snapping to Mixxx's acapella grid); crossfader at center (additive: both full) for the whole layer, not a crossfade; plan pregains and bed EQ. The vocal is started off the bed's audio-callback source clock (read_source_clock with a grid origin calibrated from beat_distance at the stopped cue), falling back to the start command's clock. In the vocal's silent pre-roll bar the residual is the median of paired source-clock reads; beyond the 30 ms guard it moves the vocal once while still silent, never mid-word (then it warns: nudge by ear). After the last word plus a bar the instrumental fades over 16 beats (gentle, never a cut); Stop (SIGTERM -> KeyboardInterrupt) fades 1.5 s. Every run ends by restoring play/volume/pregain/rate/quantize and neutral EQ/filter on decks 1-2. schedule(plan, *, bed_rate) gives the real-time offsets; dry runs print the plan and never connect. StemLayerSession runs the CLI in a child process for the GUI and parses `[layer] phase:` lines.

Human story: `user_stories/story__when_i_pick_a_vocal_and_an_instrumental_mixxx_plays_them_together_live.md`; it extends `user_stories/story__when_i_add_vocals_only_and_instrumental_only_tracks_i_layer_them_i_do_not_play_the_acapella_in_full.md`, whose rules (never a dry acapella, the bed stays live, Get Up over Outta Control is the canonical layer) still hold.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Nothing in this module renders audio; Mixxx plays the original files live.
- Target Python 3.13+.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests (`tests/test_stem_layer.py`, `tests/test_stems.py`) before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

Performs a brain.stem_layer_plan plan live through the Mixxx control API. Refuses (LayerRefused) a running mix/audition (hands.audition_transition.running_mix_processes, which also lists this module) or playing decks unless take_over. Deck 1 instrumental from its cue with set_bpm_target to the vocal's tempo; deck 2 vocal at rate 0 (the voice is never stretched); quantize and sync off on both (no snapping to Mixxx's acapella grid); crossfader at center (additive: both full) for the whole layer, not a crossfade; plan pregains and bed EQ. The vocal is started off the bed's audio-callback source clock (read_source_clock with a grid origin calibrated from beat_distance at the stopped cue), falling back to the start command's clock. In the vocal's silent pre-roll bar the residual is the median of paired source-clock reads; beyond the 30 ms guard it moves the vocal once while still silent, never mid-word (then it warns: nudge by ear). After the last word plus a bar the instrumental fades over 16 beats (gentle, never a cut); Stop (SIGTERM -> KeyboardInterrupt) fades 1.5 s. Every run ends by restoring play/volume/pregain/rate/quantize and neutral EQ/filter on decks 1-2. schedule(plan, *, bed_rate) gives the real-time offsets; dry runs print the plan and never connect. StemLayerSession runs the CLI in a child process for the GUI and parses `[layer] phase:` lines.
